# @mirror/store/action_cache — the REAPI ActionCache surface
# for verdict memoization. Sibling species under @mirror/store
# alongside @mirror/store/git (wire) and @mirror/store/crystal
# (settled artifact). N2 TICK 1 of the N-cascade.
#
# THE CLAIM: this species is the OPERATIONAL SURFACE that
# realizes the memoization AUTHORIZED by N1's predicate
# `@epistemologic/property/verdict_is_content_addressed`
# (landed 2026-07-06 at `2857fb1`). Where N1 declared that
# `verdict = f(spec_oid, target_oid, inputs_oid)` is a total
# function of its three OID inputs, this species declares the
# `cache_read` + `cache_write` action pair that implements the
# memoization at store altitude.
#
# Interpretation B canonical per Seam pre-review
# `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md` §1:
# narrative ABOVE `---`; `in` clauses + typed declarations BELOW.
#
# === Bazel REAPI ActionCache ancestor ===
#
# THE CANONICAL PRIOR-ART ANCHOR. Per M6 TICK 1 enrichment at
# `shards/mirror/store.mirror` §"Bazel REAPI floor decomposition":
# the industrial minimum floor decomposes into two orthogonal
# open surfaces the Bazel Remote Execution API (REAPI) codified:
#
#   (1) OID -> object map — the Content-Addressable Storage (CAS)
#       surface. Byte-in / byte-out; hash-mediated identity.
#       Lives at @mirror/store's canonical six-op surface
#       (read / write / exists / diff / walk / verify) IS REAPI's
#       `ContentAddressableStorage`.
#
#   (2) action-hash -> OID map — the action-cache surface. Given a
#       canonical action key (oid of the canonicalized action
#       description) return the previously-recorded output oids.
#       IS REAPI's `ActionCache`. THIS SPECIES.
#
# @mirror/store is the CAS; @mirror/store/action_cache is the
# action-hash -> verdict map at substrate altitude. The split is
# orthogonal to the scheduler (per Mokhov/Mitchell/Peyton Jones
# "Build Systems à la Carte" JFP 2020); any scheduler discipline
# (topological / restarting / suspending) composes with this
# action-cache floor. Both surfaces are Apache-2.0 open.
#
# Forward-promise from `shards/mirror/store.mirror` M6 TICK 3
# §"Bazel REAPI floor decomposition": the action-cache surface
# is "forward-promised at M6 tick 3 as sub-prism
# `@mirror/store/action_cache`". LANDING here at N2 TICK 1.
#
# === Recognition #43 grounding (mirror IS content-addressed build system) ===
#
# Per `[[architecture-mirror-as-content-addressed-build-system]]`
# (#43 LANDED at M6 TICK 1 `884f433`): mirror has every Bazel /
# Buck2 / Nix / Shake primitive declared at substrate altitude.
# The action-cache primitive was declared at Bazel's REAPI floor
# (2018+); mirror's altitude-4 form of the same primitive lives
# HERE at @mirror/store/action_cache. This shard closes the last
# unlanded Bazel-REAPI-floor-decomposition sub-prism.
#
# === The three-OID key discipline ===
#
# The cache is keyed on the same triple N1's predicate is signed
# on: `(spec_oid, target_oid, inputs_oid) -> verdict`. Each OID
# names one axis of the verdict's addressing:
#
#   - `spec_oid: oid` — the content-address of the property
#     specification (the shard declaring the predicate whose
#     verdict we cache); resolved through @mirror/store's CAS.
#   - `target_oid: oid` — the content-address of the object
#     under verdict (the artifact / crystal / splinter the
#     predicate is evaluated against); resolved through
#     @mirror/store's CAS.
#   - `inputs_oid: oid` — the content-address of the composed
#     input bundle (dependency closure OIDs, environment OIDs,
#     ancestor verdicts folded in); the canonical hash of the
#     inputs that participated in producing the verdict.
#
# The three OIDs together are the complete addressing of a
# verdict. Nothing else participates. Because N1 declared that
# verdict is a total function of the triple, this cache is
# well-formed by construction: same triple -> same verdict,
# always. No invalidation heuristic; no generational counter;
# no mtime probe. Idempotent cache_write is a consequence of the
# total-function invariant N1 anchored.
#
# === @mirror/store/crystal.derived_predicates carrier composition ===
#
# THE CARRIER THE ACTIONS READ/WRITE INTO. Per
# `shards/mirror/store/crystal.mirror` (LANDED 2026-06-16, 19KB):
# the `crystal` record's third field is
#
#   derived_predicates: [property_verdict]
#
# where `property_verdict = { verdict: verdict, where: location }`
# (per @glass). N1's declaration lifted this field from
# "audit-trail of what was verified" to "memoizable cache by
# construction" — each `property_verdict` entry becomes a
# key/value pair in the content-addressed verdict cache once the
# location keys off the input OID triple.
#
# This species DECLARES THE SURFACE that reads/writes into the
# `derived_predicates` list. `cache_read` looks up the triple
# among the crystal's derived_predicates entries; `cache_write`
# appends a new (verdict, where=triple) entry when the loop
# issues a fresh verdict. The derived_predicates carrier IS the
# substrate-decl'd cache storage; this species IS the
# substrate-decl'd cache access.
#
# === Family-root six-op composition ===
#
# This species inherits the canonical six-op surface from
# @mirror/store (`read` / `write` / `exists` / `diff` / `walk` /
# `verify`) per the `in @mirror/store` clause below. The cache
# actions DISCHARGE against that six-op surface at the
# derived_predicates carrier:
#
#   cache_read(spec, target, inputs)
#     <= walk(crystal_root)                # traverse to derived_predicates
#      + read(derived_predicates_oid)       # fetch the [property_verdict] list
#      + linear_scan_for_triple(entries, key=(spec, target, inputs))
#                                          # match entry.where against triple
#     -> imperfect(verdict, opacity)
#         success:  hit — the cached verdict for the triple
#         partial:  the triple matched but confidence is degraded
#                    (stale-cache hint; @mirror/store six-op semantics)
#         failure:  miss — no matching entry; caller runs kintsugi loop
#
#   cache_write(spec, target, inputs, v)
#     <= walk(crystal_root)                # find the derived_predicates carrier
#      + read(derived_predicates_oid)       # fetch existing list
#      + append(entries, { verdict: v,
#                          where: location_of(spec, target, inputs) })
#      + write(new_derived_predicates_bytes) # content-addressed new oid
#      + set_ref(crystal_head, new_oid)     # ref update the crystal head
#     -> verdict
#         pass:     write succeeded; new derived_predicates oid live
#         partial:  write succeeded but ref-update was contended
#                    (rare; documented at @mirror/store.write semantics)
#         failure:  I/O failure; caller retries or bails
#
#   cache_exists(spec, target, inputs)
#     <= cache_read(spec, target, inputs).is_success
#     -> verdict (hit/miss check without fetching the full verdict)
#
# The six-op surface stays canonical at @mirror/store; the
# cache verbs stay canonical at this species altitude; the
# discharge map above names the bridge (same shape as
# @mirror/store/git's wire-verb -> six-op discharge map).
#
# === Operational target: the 13-minute pre-commit hook ===
#
# Business context (Taut scout report + N1's operational target
# §): the pre-commit hook takes ~13 minutes because
# `cmd_kintsugi_spec` at `bootstrap/src/lib.rs:~1189` walks every
# target on every invocation and spawns `cargo <check>` cold each
# time. Zero cross-invocation cache; zero per-target result
# memoization.
#
# This species is the substrate-decl'd surface the N3 Rust wiring
# will consume. Once landed:
#
#   1. `cmd_kintsugi_spec` calls `cache_read(spec_oid, target_oid,
#      inputs_oid)` before dispatching cargo.
#   2. On cache hit (imperfect::success carrying the cached
#      verdict): skip cargo; re-emit the verdict.
#   3. On cache miss (imperfect::failure): run cargo; call
#      `cache_write(spec_oid, target_oid, inputs_oid, v)` to
#      record the fresh verdict; emit.
#
# The hook overhead falls from ~13 minutes to seconds on the
# second invocation because incremental verdict caching is now
# valid by construction. Recognition #43 supplies the principled
# ancestor; the pre-commit hook supplies the empirical pull.
#
# === N-cascade forward-promises ===
#
# This shard is N2 TICK 1 of the N-cascade. N1 landed the
# predicate; N2 lands the operational surface. Downstream
# N-cascade ticks the surface enables:
#
#   - N3: Rust wiring at `bootstrap/src/lib.rs:~1189` —
#         `cmd_kintsugi_spec` consults `cache_read` before
#         dispatching cargo, calls `cache_write` after each
#         fresh verdict. The 13-minute hook overhead falls
#         empirically once N3 lands.
#
#   - N4: reverse closure `impacted_by(oid) -> [oid]` at
#         @mirror/store. When an OID changes, the reverse-closure
#         walk names every downstream OID whose cached verdict
#         may be affected. Composes with cache_read at this
#         species to invalidate exactly the impacted verdict
#         entries (partial(opacity_map) on the impacted triples).
#
#   - N5: `@kintsugi/store/git commit-as-fold` — `mirror
#         kintsugi --commit` IS `git commit` at git-projection
#         altitude. Every commit is a fold over the verdict
#         cache this species declares; every reverse-closure
#         walk (N4) is a rebase over the fold. The terminal tick
#         of the N-cascade at kintsugi-projection altitude.
#
# The N-cascade grounds this species as the operational hinge:
# without cache_read + cache_write declared here, N3-N5 have no
# substrate-decl surface to consume. This shard is where the
# analytical invariant N1 declared becomes an executable contract.
#
# === Bilateral discipline per Recognition #53 ===
#
# Per `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]` (#53): the
# declarative half at `@epistemologic/property/verdict_is_content_addressed`
# (N1) pairs with an operational half. This species is the
# store-side operational half — the surface where the
# memoization invariant is DISCHARGED at read/write altitude.
# A separate `@kintsugi/fracture/verdict_cache_miss` (or
# equivalent naming) forward-promised at N3 is the fracture-side
# operational half for the case where cache_read returns
# `failure(miss)` and the kintsugi loop must re-issue the
# verdict. The bilateral pair (property + fracture) is now
# complete on the store side with this landing.
#
# === Interpretation B canonical (green-field species) ===
#
# First non-empty line = `#`-narrative; exactly one `---` seam at
# column 0; `in @...` clauses BELOW seam. Follows the sibling
# @mirror/store/git shape at `shards/mirror/store/git.mirror`
# (LANDED 2026-06-30, 20KB).
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-pull]]: every carrier below rides a
# type the substrate already declared. Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]:
# every action parameter is a typed newtype (`oid` from
# @mirror/store; `verdict` from @glass); no bare primitives
# escape. Per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]: the
# five-operation glass block IS the canonical declaration form.
# Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]: the cache
# actions ride the six-op surface + crystal.derived_predicates
# carrier the substrate had all along; nothing invented here.
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at `shards/mirror/store/action_cache.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/store/action_cache` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`. Depth-2 sub-prism
# under @mirror/store, sibling to `@mirror/store/git` and
# `@mirror/store/crystal`.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Bazel REAPI ActionCache   `github.com/bazelbuild/remote-apis`
#                             — the canonical action-hash -> output
#                             OID map used by every remote-execution
#                             build. `GetActionResult` +
#                             `UpdateActionResult` are the
#                             read/write pair; this species'
#                             `cache_read` + `cache_write` at
#                             substrate altitude match modulo
#                             naming.
#   Bazel Remote (buchgr)     `github.com/buchgr/bazel-remote` —
#                             the reference standalone action-cache
#                             server backing REAPI clients. Same
#                             shape at wire altitude.
#   Nix ca-derivations        the content-addressed derivation arc
#                             (Dolstra 2020-2023); action = derivation
#                             hash; output = content-address; the
#                             same total-function invariant Nix's
#                             ca-derivations arc names at the
#                             derivation altitude.
#   Buck2 dep graph           the incremental dep-graph engine
#                             (Meta, 2023) built around a
#                             content-addressed action cache;
#                             action-hash -> output-OID discipline
#                             at build-system altitude.
#
# Spec context:
#              `docs/specs/mosaic-store-cache-invariants.md`
#               (Mara 2026-06-28, 2016 lines; §9.2 forward-promises
